0,Idu Mishmi language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idu_Mishmi_language,"2 weeks ago - The Igu wears a coat, loin cloth, and an apron-like garment, and uses musical instruments while dancing, chanting, and singing. Idu Mishmi has variously been described as Sino-Tibetan or that of one part in a family termed 'Digarish', while Blench (2024) rejects both groupings, arguing that ...",Idu-Mishmi,Sino-Tibetan
1,Music of Tibet - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Tibet,"May 6, 2026 - The music of Tibet reflects the cultural heritage of the trans-Himalayan region centered in Tibet, but also known wherever Indigenous Tibetan groups are found in Nepal, Bhutan, India and further abroad. The religious music of Tibet reflects the profound influence of Tibetan Buddhism on the culture.",Idu-Mishmi,Sino-Tibetan
2,Mishmi people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mishmi_people,"May 17, 2026 - The Idus are primarily concentrated in the Upper Dibang Valley and Lower Dibang Valley district and some of the northern parts of Lohit district of Arunachal Pradesh in India. Taraon, also called Digaru Mishmis, are distributed in the hill and the foothills between the Dibang, Digaru and the ...",Idu-Mishmi,Sino-Tibetan
3,Music of Arunachal Pradesh — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Music_of_Arunachal_Pradesh,"January 14, 2026 - The music of the Monpa, Idu Mishmi, and other border tribes in Arunachal Pradesh reflects a unique fusion of Tibetan Buddhist influences and indigenous animist traditions, shaped by their proximity to the Himalayas and trans-border migrations.",Idu-Mishmi,Sino-Tibetan
4,Sino-Tibetan | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/236/,"Digaro-Mishmi mhu, a language of India · Idu-Mishmi clk, a language of India · Hrusish 2 · Hruso hru, a language of India · Miji sjl, a language of India · Keman 1 · Zakhring zkr, a language of China · Kho-Bwa 6 · Bugun bgg, a language of India · Chug cvg, a language of India ·",Idu-Mishmi,Sino-Tibetan
5,The Sound of Tibetan Pop - playlist by The Sounds of Spotify | Spotify,https://open.spotify.com/playlist/02lAxUTKaWXNEtYAIEaZpP,Playlist · The Sound of Tibetan Pop · 317 items · 243 saves,Idu-Mishmi,Sino-Tibetan
6,Songs and Music of Tibet | Smithsonian Folkways Recordings,https://folkways.si.edu/songs-and-music-of-tibet/world/album/smithsonian,"From a camp in the outskirts of Kathmandu, Howard Kaufman captures the essence of Tibetan chants. Kaufman gathers songs that are ""excerpts from much longer versions of both Eastern and Western Tibet"".",Idu-Mishmi,Sino-Tibetan
7,Understanding the importance of Tibetan music,https://www.tibettravel.org/tibetan-culture/understanding-the-importance-of-tibetan-music.html,"May 6, 2025 - You will find that flutes and lutes combine with some percussion beats to create a soft aroma of music that is thought to resemble a constant communication link with the divine world, one that only ""perfect beings"" are able to compose. It is officially named Sino-Mongolian music and is heard in the streets during festivals and parties.",Idu-Mishmi,Sino-Tibetan
8,"Idu-Mishmi Language (CLK) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map, Endangered Level & Official Use | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/clk/,"Idu-Mishmi is an endangered indigenous language of India and China. It belongs to the Sino-Tibetan language family. The language is used as a first language by all adults in the ethnic community, but not all young people.",Idu-Mishmi,Sino-Tibetan
9,"Idu Mishmi | District Lower Dibang Valley, Government of Arunachal Pradesh. | India",https://roing.nic.in/culture-heritage/idu-mishmi/,"April 8, 2026 - The IDU-MISHMI is a major sub-tribe of Mishmi group. Their brethren tribes are namely the DIGARU-MISHMI (TARAONS) and the MIJU-MISHMI (KAMANS). They inhabit the Lohit district, Dibang Valley district and Lower Dibang Valley district. They are of mongoloid stock and speak the Tibeto-Burman language.",Idu-Mishmi,Sino-Tibetan
